>> title: Pita Bread
>> servings: 8
>> author: Ted Lin
>> date: 2020-03-21
>> dish: pita
>> cuisine: Middle Eastern
>> keywords: bread, grill
>> summary: A simple, slightly sweet pita for the oven or the grill, best fresh.
>> source: http://www.thefreshloaf.com/recipes/pitabread

# Dough

:mix @{all-purpose flour|3 cups}, @{yeast|2 tsp}, @{kosher salt|1 tsp}, @{sugar|1 tbsp} in #{mixing bowl} => _dough.
:add @{olive oil|2 tbsp} and @{warm water|1 1/4 cups} to _dough, combine into a loose dough.
:{knead|about 10 min} _dough by hand until smooth.
:{rise|60-90 min} _dough in #{oiled bowl} covered with #{damp towel} until doubled; time depends on your temperature.
:punch down _dough and divide into 8 pieces => _{pita rounds|8}.
:{rest|20 min} _{pita rounds}.

# Bake

:roll _{pita rounds} to about 1/8 in thick; if they do not stretch well, let them rest a bit.
:{bake|3 min} _{pita rounds} at #{oven|400F}, flipping after about 2 min, until they puff up completely before the flip.
  (on the grill this may take much less time)

>> note: Garlic powder works, but may need additional rising time.
